cial and geographic barriers to entry. The solution is a dedicated semiconductor training and skill development center that provides affordable, industry-standard training in VL","problemStatement":"VLSI Semiconductor Skill Development addresses the limited access rural and economically disadvantaged women have to advanced technology education, while the semiconductor industry faces a growing shortage of skilled talent. Most VLSI and chip design training programs are concentrated in metropolitan areas, creating financial and geographic barriers to entry. The solution is a dedicated semiconductor training and skill development center that provides affordable, industry-standard training in VLSI design, FPGA development, verification, physical design, and semiconductor manufacturing. Through hands-on projects, industry mentorship, certifications, and placement support, the initiative aims to train 100–200 women annually, creating employment, entrepreneurship, and workforce opportunities in India’s growing semiconductor ecosystem.","proposedSolution":"","businessModel":"","expectedImpact":"","fundingRequested":0,"stage":"registration","status":"pending","bootcamp":{"attended":true,"date":"","remarks":""},"data":{"consentLetter":false,"fundingTemplate":false,"msmeRegistered":false,"msmeNumber":"","status":"pending","submittedDate":"","teamId":"cedau-50","teamSize":0,"linkedin":"","collegeLinkedin":"","domain":"Ed-Tech","domainTags":"EdTech, App Development / Software, DeepTech","session":"S8","startupRegistered":""},"rounds":{},"finalEval":{"status":"pending","decision":"","remarks":"","date":""},"edi":{"status":"not_submitted","grantReviewAppId":"","decisionDate":"","remarks":""},"bank":{"accountName":"","accountNumber":"","bankName":"","ifscCode":"","branch":""},"registration":{"udyamNumber":"","gstNumber":"","panNumber":"","registrationType":"","pitchLink":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16dmS9BkwYK-znvr3Rkj5DTs7hprWCF1E/view?usp=sharing"},"grant":{"approvalDate":"",