e, causing microplastic pollution). The global leather goods market is valued at $498.57 billion (2024), growing to $855.36 billion (2032), while the vegan leather market is $82.19 billion (2024), projected to reach $198.17 billion (2034). Chrysolux addresses this by developing mycelium-based leather combined with Black Soldier F","problemStatement":"The leather industry relies on animal leather (causing deforestation, methane emissions, and toxic tanning) and PU/PVC vegan leather (petroleum-derived, non-biodegradable, causing microplastic pollution). The global leather goods market is valued at $498.57 billion (2024), growing to $855.36 billion (2032), while the vegan leather market is $82.19 billion (2024), projected to reach $198.17 billion (2034). Chrysolux addresses this by developing mycelium-based leather combined with Black Soldier Fly chitin coating, creating a 100% biodegradable, plastic-free, chemical-free material with water resistance and antimicrobial properties","proposedSolution":"","businessModel":"","expectedImpact":"","fundingRequested":0,"stage":"registration","status":"rejected","bootcamp":{"attended":true,"date":"","remarks":""},"data":{"consentLetter":false,"fundingTemplate":false,"msmeRegistered":false,"msmeNumber":"","status":"pending","submittedDate":"","teamId":"PX-3ki6nJ","teamSize":0,"linkedin":"","collegeLinkedin":"","domain":"Enviro-Tech","domainTags":"AgriTech, Fashion / Lifestyle, Enviro Tech","session":"S5","startupRegistered":""},"rounds":{},"finalEval":{"status":"pending","decision":"","remarks":"","date":""},"edi":{"status":"not_submitted","grantReviewAppId":"","decisionDate":"","remarks":""},"bank":{"accountName":"","accountNumber":"","bankName":"","ifscCode":"","branch":""},"registration":{"udyamNumber":"","gstNumber":"","panNumber":"","registrationType":"","pitchLink":"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/17APXum_6v75puPYL7bfg9TQt7yJJxsxX/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104277249549708518105&rtpof=true&sd=true"},"grant":{"approvalDate