""},"phase3":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""}},"pitchLink":"","documents":[],"notes":[],"createdDate":"2026-09-17","lastUpdated":"2026-09-17","history":[{"date":"2026-09-17","time":"12:00","user":"System","action":"Imported from CED Excel","from":"","to":"registration","remarks":"Batch 2025-26"}]},{"applicationId":"GRT-2026-27-085","applicantName":"Prempradeep S","phone":"7708365986","email":"prempradeep038@gmail.com","memberId":null,"teamId":"SC-b4jkfxa","type":"team","batch":"2025-26","gender":"Male","caste":"General","tier":"Tier 1","college":"R.M.K. Engineering College","womenBeneficiaries":1,"ideaName":"Aquaholics","sector":"Industry 4.0","industry":"Industry 4.0","ideaDescription":"Aquaholics Autonomous Water Surface Cleaning Robot addresses plastic pollution crisis in water ecosystems threatening marine life and water quality, where India relies primarily on slow, expensive, risky manual labor that misses debris in hard-to-reach areas, while semi-automated/robotic systems fail at waste handling, obstacle navigation, and bad weather performance—making consistent cleaning difficult for municipalities/NGOs. The 25kg-capacity robot features autonomous navigation via LiDAR/GPS","problemStatement":"Aquaholics Autonomous Water Surface Cleaning Robot addresses plastic pollution crisis in water ecosystems threatening marine life and water quality, where India relies primarily on slow, expensive, risky manual labor that misses debris in hard-to-reach areas, while semi-automated/robotic systems fail at waste handling, obstacle navigation, and bad weather performance—making consistent cleaning difficult for municipalities/NGOs. The 25kg-capacity robot features autonomous navigation via LiDAR/GPS/IMU+SLAM+ROS for real-time mapping, computer vision/polarized cameras for waste detection (plastics/debris/oil spills), screw conveyor+robotic arm for collection, 360° ballast tanks for stability, hybrid solar/battery power, pH/DO/water level sensors, acoustic deterrence for aquatic safety, UV disinfection, and LoRa communication—reducing manual labor costs while preserving biodiversity.​","proposedSolution":"","businessModel":"","expectedImpact":"","fundingRequested":1000,"stage":"grant","status":"selected","bootcamp":{"attended":true,"date":"","remarks":""},"data":{"consentLetter":false,"fundingTemplate":false,"msmeRegistered":false,"msmeNumber":"","status":"pending","submittedDate":"","teamId":"SC-b4jkfxa","teamSize":13,"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/prem-pradeep-s","collegeLinkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/school/r.m.k-engineering-college/","domain":"Deep-Tech","domainTags":"AI / ML , IoT / Hardware, Deep Tech, Robotics / Automation","session":"S3","startupRegistered":"-"},"rounds":{},"finalEval":{"status":"pending","decision":"","remarks":"","date":""},"edi":{"status":"not_submitted","grantReviewAppId":"","decisionDate":"","remarks":""},"bank":{"accountName":"","accountNumber":"","bankName":"","ifscCode":"","branch":""},"registration":{"udyamNumber":"","gstNumber":"","panNumber":"","registrationType":"","pitchLink":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VorSWnUlyM-hZbEwKD3-ydU3amct_rNZ/view?usp=sharing"},"grant":{"approvalDate":"","sanctionLetterNo":"","approvedAmount":1000,"grantType":"Grant Fund","bankVerification":"Pending","agreementStatus":"Pending","phase1":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""},"phase2":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""},"phase3":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""}},"pitchLink":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VorSWnUlyM-hZbEwKD3-ydU3amct_rNZ/view?usp=sharing","documents":[],"notes":[],"createdDate":"2026-09-17","lastUpdated":"2026-09-17","history":[{"date":"2026-09-17","time":"12:00","user":"System","action":"Imported from CED Excel","from":"","to":"grant","remarks":"Batch 2025-26"}]},{"applicationId":"GRT-2026-27-086","applicantName":"Antanet Anusha G","phone":"9384233122","email":"anuthiraviam@gmail.com","memberId":null,"teamId":"Px-xocu6","type":"individual","batch":"2025-26","gender":"Female","caste":"OBC","tier":"Tier 3","college":"Alagappa College of Technology","womenBeneficiaries":0,"ideaName":"Millet-Based Electrolyte Beverages","sector":"Food tech","industry":"Food tech","ideaDescription":"Commercial electrolyte drinks suffer from high sugar content (20–35g per serving), costly premium options 40–60% more expensive, single-use PET plastic packaging, and high water/carbon footprints in a USD 42.6B global market (2024) projected to USD 74.2B by 2034, driving obesity, diabetes, and metabolic risks especially among athletes, children, diabetics, and low-income consumers. The millet-based electrolyte beverage solution uses controlled germination of millets (finger/proso) to activate ph","problemStatement":"Commercial electrolyte drinks suffer from high sugar content (20–35g per serving), costly premium options 40–60% more expensive, single-use PET plastic packaging, and high water/carbon footprints in a USD 42.6B global market (2024) projected to USD 74.2B by 2034, driving obesity, diabetes, and metabolic risks especially among athletes, children, diabetics, and low-income consumers. The millet-based electrolyte beverage solution uses controlled germination of millets (finger/proso) to activate phytase for 2–3× higher natural mineral absorption (Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, Fe²⁺, Zn²⁺), delivers low-glycemic hydration with prebiotic oligosaccharides, antioxidants, gut health support, and 70% less water usage in a sustainable, clean-label formulation safe for diabetics/children.","proposedSolution":"","businessModel":"","expectedImpact":"","fundingRequested":0,"stage":"registration","status":"pending","bootcamp":{"attended":true,"date":"","remarks":""},"data":{"consentLetter":false,"fundingTemplate":false,"msmeRegistered":false,"msmeNumber":"","status":"pending","submittedDate":"","teamId":"Px-xocu6","teamSize":0,"linkedin":"","collegeLinkedin":"","domain":"Food tech","domainTags":"Bio Tech, Food Tech","session":"S4","startupRegistered":""},"rounds":{},"finalEval":{"status":"pending","decision":"","remarks":"","date":""},"edi":{"status":"not_submitted","grantReviewAppId":"","decisionDate":"","remarks":""},"bank":{"accountName":"","accountNumber":"","bankName":"","ifscCode":"","branch":""},"registration":{"udyamNumber":"","gstNumber":"","panNumber":"","registrationType":"","pitchLink":"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1GTUuQ193iH8aPr4qTGOjSh7oj8tF1aN7/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104277249549708518105&rtpof=true&sd=true"},"grant":{"approvalDate":"","sanctionLetterNo":"","approvedAmount":0,"grantType":"Grant Fund","bankVerification":"Pending","agreementStatus":"Pending","phase1":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""},"phase2":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""},"phase3":{"amount":0,"eligibleAmount":0,"releaseDate":"","status":"pending","refNumber":"","remarks":""}},"pitchLink":"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1GTUuQ193iH8aPr4qTGOjSh7oj8tF1aN7/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104277249549708518105&rtpof=true&sd=true","documents":[],"notes":[],"createdDate":"2026-09-17","lastUpdated":"2026-09-17","history":[{"date":"2026-09-17","time":"12:00","user":"System","action":"Imported from CED Excel","from":"","to":"registration","remarks":"Batch 2025-26"}]},{"applicationId":"GRT-2026-27-087","applicantName":"Tharaneeswharan","phone":"9361054415","email":"tharaneeswharan5555@gmail.com","memberId":null,"teamId":"SC-07g6mo","type":"individual","batch":"2025-26","gender":"Male","caste":"General","tier":"Tier 3","college":"Velalar College of Engineering and Technology","womenBeneficiaries":0,"ideaName":"UZHAVAN","sector":"Enviro-Tech","industry":"Enviro-Tech","ideaDescription":"India produces over 20,000 tons of expired/unused pharmaceutical waste annually, mostly incinerated or dumped, causing soil toxicity, water contamination, and increasing antimicrobial resistance, while farmers simultaneously struggle with expensive chemical fertilizers lacking affordable organic alternatives—creating a dual crisis requiring circular, eco-friendly solutions. Uzhavan''s BioReclaim transforms this crisis into opportunity through an AI-powered circular system: AI-powered machines sep","problemStatement":"India produces over 20,000 tons of expired/unused pharmaceutical waste annually, mostly incinerated or dumped, causing soil toxicity, water contamination, and increasing antimicrobial resistance, while farmers simultaneously struggle with expensive chemical fertilizers lacking affordable organic alternatives—creating a dual crisis requiring circular, eco-friendly solutions. Uzhavan''s BioReclaim transforms this crisis into opportunity through an AI-powered circular system: AI-powered machines separate tablets from blister packs, tablets are pulverized and mixed with cow dung at 1:10 ratio, natural microbes neutralize harmful compounds during controlled bioremediation and composting (70-90 days), producing safe, nutrient-rich organic fertilizer—offering AI-powered tablet sorting (automation reducing manual error), bioremediation with cow dung microbes (toxin neutralization + nutrient enrichment vs. incineration/landfill), dual impact (simultaneous pharma waste disposal + affordable fertilizer), modular & scalable units (1-ton/month plants replicable near pharma hubs/rural areas), and 5x cost advantage (cheaper than imported waste-to-fertilizer systems)—generating impact across waste reduction, eco-friendly fertilizer production, farmer support, public health (reduced antimicrobial resistance), rural employment, and alignment with Swachh Bharat & Atmanirbhar Bharat national goals, validated by experienced farmers (20, 40, 62-year farming backgrounds).​","proposedSolution":"","business