lacking affordable diagnostic tools because current methods (PCR/ELISA) are expensive, time-consuming, inaccessible, and detect infections too late to prevent damage. GenéGlow''s \"Fluorza\" solution uses genetically engineered Pseudomonas fluorescens bacteria integrated with CRISPR-Cas9 technology to detect crop viral infections on-site within 24–4","problemStatement":"Plant viruses cause $60 billion+ in annual global agricultural losses (FAO), threatening food security and farmer livelihoods, with smallholder farmers lacking affordable diagnostic tools because current methods (PCR/ELISA) are expensive, time-consuming, inaccessible, and detect infections too late to prevent damage. GenéGlow''s \"Fluorza\" solution uses genetically engineered Pseudomonas fluorescens bacteria integrated with CRISPR-Cas9 technology to detect crop viral infections on-site within 24–48 hours through visible UV fluorescence, offering an affordable (₹100/unit) spray requiring no laboratory expertise or infrastructure, with built-in environmental \"kill switch\" biosafety and scalability across multiple crops and viral pathogens, empowering resource-limited farmers while reducing chemical pesticide dependency and promoting sustainable farming practices.","proposedSolution":"","businessModel":"","expectedImpact":"","fundingRequested":0,"stage":"registration","status":"rejected","bootcamp":{"attended":true,"date":"","remarks":""},"data":{"consentLetter":false,"fundingTemplate":false,"msmeRegistered":false,"msmeNumber":"","status":"pending","submittedDate":"","teamId":"SC-oyp2ts","teamSize":0,"linkedin":"","collegeLinkedin":"","domain":"Agri-Tech","domainTags":"Bio Tech, AgriTech, Enviro Tech","session":"S4","startupRegistered":""},"rounds":{},"finalEval":{"status":"pending","decision":"","remarks":"","date":""},"edi":{"status":"not_submitted","grantReviewAppId":"","decisionDate":"","remarks":""},"bank":{"accountName":"","accountNumber":"","bankName":"","ifscCode":"","branch":""},"registratio