stem","action":"Imported from CED Excel","from":"","to":"registration","remarks":"Batch 2026-27"}]},{"applicationId":"GRT-2026-27-161","applicantName":"Faheera Umu Salma","phone":"8681879364","email":"Fahi1709@gmail.com","memberId":null,"teamId":"SC(BT)-fFRV5","type":"individual","batch":"2025-26","gender":"Female","caste":"General","tier":"Tier 1","college":"Alagappa College of Technology","womenBeneficiaries":0,"ideaName":"Diagnobee","sector":"Med-Tech","industry":"Med-Tech","ideaDescription":"Silent heart attacks go unnoticed in 45% of cases worldwide, with high risk in diabetics, elderly, and women, while current diagnostic tests (ECG, troponin) miss early signs and detect damage only after occurrence, leading to disabilities and high healthcare costs. DiagnoBee''s CardioSense patch addresses this with a painless microneedle-based device that detects early cardiac microRNAs (miR-208a, miR-133a, miR-499-5p) released before troponins appear, using aptamer technology for specific bindin","problemStatement":"Silent heart attacks go unnoticed in 45% of cases worldwide, with high risk in diabetics, elderly, and women, while current diagnostic tests (ECG, troponin) miss early signs and detect damage only after occurrence, leading to disabilities and high healthcare costs. DiagnoBee''s CardioSense patch addresses this with a painless microneedle-based device that detects early cardiac microRNAs (miR-208a, miR-133a, miR-499-5p) released before troponins appear, using aptamer technology for specific binding and fluorescent UV-based detection—offering multiplex detection of three markers on a single strip in ~20 minutes without lab infrastructure or skilled staff, at ₹490 per unit cost with portable smartphone app readout for self-monitoring and clinical verification options, enabling scalable access for rural health programs, ambulances, and primary health centers.​","proposedSolution":"","businessModel":"","expectedImpact":"","fundingRequested":0,"stage":"registration","